# Accepted HIGH advisories — read by the Trivy image scan and by scripts/audit-gate.js (npm audit).
# Every entry needs a reason in SECURITY.md ("Residual advisories") and an exp: date; an expired
# entry is enforced again. List the GHSA id (npm audit) and the CVE id (Trivy).

# zod 3.x (Zod memory exhaustion on oversized constrained collections). Pulled in only by kaibanjs
# 0.24.2 (latest) through @kaibanjs/workflow, @langchain/openai 0.5, openai 4–5 and stagehand; no
# patched 3.x exists and those packages declare zod ^3 (dependency or peer). Kaiban's own code uses
# zod 4.6.7 (patched). Re-check on every kaibanjs release.
GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2026-12-31

# picomatch <= 4.0.7 (ReDoS on single-branch repeated extglob patterns). Development tooling only:
# vitest, vite and tinyglobby, in the root and the board lockfiles. Not in the published package and
# not in the container image (`npm ci --omit=dev`); the patterns it matches come from the test and
# build configuration of this repository, not from user input. No patched version exists yet
# (4.0.7 is the latest). Re-check weekly; remove this entry when a fixed version is released.
